WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.340
Hi, I'm Rowan!

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:05.488
Adapt-1 Machina trains a simulated arm with no critic.

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:07.237
What does the critic's job?

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:14.246
The simulator is the critic: propose a whole command sequence, run it,

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:16.299
grade it, and revise earlier attempts.

00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:20.165
An attempt is one matrix.

00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:21.638
Each row is a command.

00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:23.397
Three numbers place the tool,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:25.716
three turn it,

00:00:27.762 --> 00:00:29.083
and one sets the gripper.

00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:34.180
Up to twenty rows, a hundred and forty numbers, committed before the arm moves.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:40.026
Propose the whole matrix at once: one decision per attempt, not per step.

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.176
Run it in the simulator.

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:43.907
Nothing estimates its value first.

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:49.169
Hand-written detectors grade it: contact, lift, transfer, and a placement that stays put.

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:54.203
Then revise a recorded attempt: keep its opening, change a few indexed numbers.

00:00:55.842 --> 00:00:57.387
One part is learned.

00:00:57.387 --> 00:01:00.477
It reads the starting observation through quadratic features.

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:04.150
It outputs a bounded correction, from weights that start at zero.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:08.294
It's added to the sequence the search found, and clipped to the allowed range.

00:01:09.842 --> 00:01:13.098
That correction at work, in the lab's own recordings: before it on

00:01:13.098 --> 00:01:14.726
the left, after on the right.

00:01:15.146 --> 00:01:18.200
A few centimetres more on the release, and the cube lands in

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.727
the bowl, not on its rim.

00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:26.487
Feed it another case's observation and it does worse than none: sixty-two against eighty-five.

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:28.414
It really reads the observation.

00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:34.361
On three hundred and eighty-four unseen layouts, placements rose six point two

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:36.745
five points: seventy gained, forty-six lost.

00:01:36.745 --> 00:01:39.130
Its interval starts under one point.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:44.581
No critic doesn't mean no cost: the simulator does the critic's job,

00:01:44.581 --> 00:01:46.550
one executed attempt at a time.

00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:53.348
Propose a matrix, let the simulator grade it, edit, and learn one small correction.

00:01:53.768 --> 00:01:55.794
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:55.794 --> 00:01:56.373
I'm Rowan.

00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:56.663
Bye!
